<input_test_case_set_format>
A test case set contains an abstract execution sequence with test steps, variables, values, and a step_type.
The test case set template is structured as follows:

```
{TestCaseSetName}
    {Step 1}    step_type:flow
    {Step 2}    param_name=${parameter_value}    step_type:flow
    {Step 3}    'value'    step_type:flow
    {Step 4}    param_name=${parameter_value}    step_type:check
    ...
```

Explanations:
- param_name is the name of a parameter,
- ${param_value} is the placeholder for its corresponding value
- Concrete parameter values are resolved in the parameter data table; do NOT flag their absence as an error.
- step_type can be flow (action) or check (validation).
- Values are formatted as Python representation: 'value'.
- If a parameter has multiple variables, they are interpreted as a list.
- The value "-" indicates null values.
</input_test_case_set_format>

<abstract_test_case_set>
Consider the following step sequence of a test case set:
```
{{ agent.step_sequence }}
```
</abstract_test_case_set>

<parameter_data>
Additionally, the following parameter data is contained in this test case set:
The table has a header row specifying the parameter names.
Each subsequent row represents a concrete test case with a combination of parameter values.

```
{{ agent.parameter_combinations }}
```
</parameter_data>

<task>
Create a description for this test case set consisting solely of the test objective.
Test objective: Summarise the main goal of the abstract test case set in one sentence.
</task>

<output_format>
Use the following format for the description.
It must be in plain text:
```
{Test objective} ("This test case set verifies ...")
...
```

- Remove leading whitespace and line breaks before the text.
- Do not alter any proper nouns, test step names, parameter names, parameter values, values, etc. from the input.

</output_format>